# tier: original-diagnostic
# oracle: independent-derivation
# scenario: diag-stic-cstack-pass
# profile: intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
# program: fixtures/FX-diag-stic-1/diag-stic-1.listing.txt (ivs-diag-stic-1), entered through
#   fixtures/FX-boot-stub/boot-stub.listing.txt (contract 1: J $5000 with R6 = 0340)
#
# Predicate of ivs-diag-stic-1, Color Stack path (D-20, D-02, A-04): the guest state at the stop and the
# first completed frame, derived by hand in plan 06-01 (docs/video/diag-stic-1-derivation.md, sections (b),
# (c) and (d); the frame literal data/video/frames/F-D2.frame with its sha256-text key; the card rules
# of data/stic/rules.json and docs/video/frame-derivations.md), BEFORE the program, the scenario, the
# STIC code or any run existed; it moves here with the scenario. It was not generated by, read back from
# or edited to match the core or a run. The author of this derivation also wrote the register literal,
# the card rules, the frames, the program and the core, so all of them can share one misreading of a
# source; agreement among them is not independent evidence about hardware. The card layouts rest on one
# community page (C96), the register roles on the same page (C81), and every window and bus figure is a
# default (C1, C2, C92); the claims that rest on this file stay provisional for that reason.
# Excluded on purpose: machine time (printed in the report, never asserted), the frame tick, all CPU
# registers, R7 and the flags (C40, C45, C56), the stack word [0340] (C68), the graphics RAM contents
# (not readable by the CPU at the stop) and the number of bus windows.
#
# derivation: mode. KEY_1 closed alone from tick 0: the first read of 01FE returns the low byte 7E, so the branch is not taken and the read of 0021 selects Color Stack mode; the recorded port byte is [02F1] = 007E.
# derivation: state. The program stores the end marker 03C5 at 02F0 last, the six explicit card words at
#   BACKTAB cells (8,3) 02A3 = 2A01, (8,4) 02A4 = 0E0A, (8,5) 02A5 = 1A13, (8,6) 02A6 = 381C, (11,0)
#   02DC = 2C1D and (11,19) 02EF = 1C0F, and fills the other cells with 0000 (checked at 0200).
# derivation: frame. The display strobe lands about cycle 95 of the frame, the stack registers, the 32
#   pattern bytes and every BACKTAB word are in place long before the row latches (cycle 3,848 + 912 x row
#   at the earliest), the guest stops between the first and the second frame end, so frame 0 is displayed
#   and the one delivered frame equals F-D2.frame. Pixels are listed by plane position (x 0 to 158, y 0
#   to 95; a card cell (r,c) starts at x = 8c, y = 8r) as an index 0 to 15 and are read from the card
#   rules and the cell lines of F-D2.frame, then compared with its plane: the pattern bytes are the
#   box, stripes, diagonal and checker shapes of the derivation (project-authored).
# Body: one assert per clause in the runner's scenario grammar, hex upper case, exact compare, evaluated
# at the stop, in the order of data/scenarios/diag-stic-cstack-pass.ivss (golden-expect-drift).
assert halted == yes
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 007E
assert mem 02A3 == 2A01
assert mem 02A4 == 0E0A
assert mem 02A5 == 1A13
assert mem 02A6 == 381C
assert mem 02DC == 2C1D
assert mem 02EF == 1C0F
assert mem 0200 == 0000
assert frame 0 displayed == yes
# pixel (0,0): the fill word 0000 in Color Stack mode shows stack entry 0 (6)
assert frame 0 pixel 0 0 == 6
# pixel (158,0): top right corner, the same fill
assert frame 0 pixel 158 0 == 6
# pixel (24,64): cell (8,3) stripes, row 0 set, foreground 1
assert frame 0 pixel 24 64 == 1
# pixel (24,65): cell (8,3) row 1 clear, stack entry 1 (A) after its advance bit
assert frame 0 pixel 24 65 == 10
# pixel (41,65): cell (8,5) diagonal, foreground 11 (bit 12 is foreground bit 3)
assert frame 0 pixel 41 65 == 11
# pixel (48,64): cell (8,6) checker AA, row 0 first pixel set, foreground 12
assert frame 0 pixel 48 64 == 12
# pixel (49,64): cell (8,6) second pixel clear, stack entry 2 (3) after its advance bit
assert frame 0 pixel 49 64 == 3
# pixel (0,88): cell (11,0) checker AA, row 0 first pixel set, foreground 5
assert frame 0 pixel 0 88 == 5
# pixel (1,88): cell (11,0) second pixel clear, stack entry 3 (D) after its advance bit
assert frame 0 pixel 1 88 == 13
# pixel (152,88): cell (11,19) box row 0, foreground 15
assert frame 0 pixel 152 88 == 15
# pixel (153,89): cell (11,19) row 1 interior clear, stack entry 3 (D)
assert frame 0 pixel 153 89 == 13
# hash: the text hash equals the sha256-text key of F-D2.frame (the gate step video ties the two)
assert frame 0 hash == f003c96b3a0cd25c77701694a1a1e7286b47b214e073275f6a58395fd6705f1c
assert video count == 1
